# Python
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Audio test artifacts
*.wav

# ONNX models — run brain/tools/fetch_models.py instead
brain/models/

# Who Humalien has met. Local to each machine, never committed.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- 3D, and the one rule here that is a licence and not a preference -----
#
# The head mesh is royalty-free under a No AI licence: free to use in the
# build, not free to redistribute, and never to be fed to a generative 3D
# tool. It stays out of git entirely — cad/head_ref.py reproduces the
# import and scaling from wherever you keep the file locally.
**/female_human_head.*

# Anyone else's models, kept locally as a measuring reference and not ours
# to redistribute. Extension-based on purpose, so it holds wherever they land.
*.3mf
*.step
*.obj
*.mtl
*.fbx

# Blender working files, including the .blend1/.blend2 rolling backups and any
# hand-made safety copy. HEAD_FACE and HEAD_CRANIUM live inside these and are
# cut from the No-AI-licence sculpt above, so the file is not ours to
# redistribute. It is also 50+ MB of binary that git cannot diff.
# What is NOT reproducible - the USERFIX_HEAD_CRANIUM hand edit - is a
# liability precisely because it only exists here. See commit 30235e1.
*.blend
*.blend[0-9]

# Exports are build output and are NOT tracked in v2. v1 tracked them, on the
# reasoning that having the exact file that was printed is useful - and it
# was, twice. What it also did was leave superseded STLs in the working tree
# next to current ones, so which file to print became a question you had to
# answer from git rather than from the folder. Two of them were printed from
# after being superseded.
#
# The deciding argument is the licence, not the clutter: the head shells are
# cut straight from the No-AI sculpt, exporting them is fine and committing
# them is redistribution. Ignoring the whole folder removes the chance of
# getting that wrong by hand.
#
# cad/rack.py and cad/eye_v2.py rebuild every part, and cad/checks.py gates
# them before any of it reaches a bed.
exports/
print/
*.stl

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
